 to go  to get help I think the good news here  is the awareness has never been better  the question is still though what is  pushing this issue and you have a good  sense of that nicka Sal what is pushing  this issue is it the increased assaults  against police complaints of misconduct  I think it's everything there there is  both the pressures seeing the calamity  and horrors during your tour the stigmas  that work the you know pressure from  from the public and the administration's  pressure to always be right I mean it's  a very stressful job being a police  officer and I think that we you know as  Chuck Russell said you know we have to  look at this we have to analyze it but  you know Pat Lynch again with the PBA is  touting more outside the department I  don't agree with the way the former  police commissioner Jimmy O'Neil handled  it  I think that they should be looking for  to help the rank-and-file you have to go  to the people the rank-and-file admire  and respect and that's the unions need  to have a larger part of this all right  well when I hear more about this Nick  Cassell Chuck veksler Karen Salomon  thank you all for being here tonight to  help us understand this very disturbing  trend among America's law enforcement  officers up next our shoutout for the  reporter whose work led to the  resignation this week of a powerful  member of Congress Republican  congressman Duncan Hunter of California  resigned this week from Congress without  offering an explanation of why but as we  first reported last year the why was no  secret to readers of the San Diego  union-tribune  where reporter Morgan Cooke spent more  than a year investigating how the  congressman was breaking the law by  using campaign money as a personal piggy  bank it was a thousand dollars spent on  video games that led to the downfall of  a popular California Republican  congressman congressman Duncan Hunter  blamed his teenage son saying he  mistakenly build some $1,300 to his  campaign instead of using the family's  personal credit card but at the San  Diego Union Tribune reporter Morgan cook  wasn't buying that excuse as she  discovered other questionable  expenditures in the records the  congressman had filed a church for oral  and facial surgery we saw new garage  door there were strange patterns of  charges lots of gas stations lots of  grocery stores just a fast-food a $229  charge at the star trader store at  Disneyland that the congressman claimed  was for food and beverages for the  campaign so I call and I'm like what  kind of food do you guys had and I said  well we have Pez and a Star War themed  rice krispies treat and I was like wow  somebody's gonna have a tummy ache  prosecutors would later document of  $9,200  to Italy for Hunter and his wife  Margaret who also pleaded guilty to a  criminal count along with traveled to  Hawaii resorts in Arizona money spent in  Washington allegedly to pay for a series  of extramarital affairs even $600 in  airfare for the family pet rabbit named  Egbert Cook says she knew almost  immediately she was on to something big  you know we couldn't really let it go  it's like every question we answered  there was another question and another  question and everywhere we looked there  was another question so he couldn't  really let up hunter first elected in  2008 and succeeding his father of the  same name was a well-known and popular  figure in the halls of Congress and as  prosecutors closed in he said he was  being investigated for what were only  accounting mistakes calling it a  witch-hunt aimed at him because he was  an outspoken defender of President Trump  they could try to have a political  agenda as our law enforcement as a US  government I think we've we've seen with  strong and and with the FBI and the DOJ  have been doing let's let them expose  themselves for what they are and that's  a politically motivated group of folks  but late last year the congressman  changed his tune pleading guilty to one  count of conspiracy to convert campaign  funds to personal use likely to face  time in prison when he is sentenced  later this year I failed to monitor and  account for my campaign spending I made  mistakes and that's what today was all  about the federal prosecutor on the case  Phil Halpern said there was nothing  political about it that the  investigation began only after he read  the reporting by Morgan Cooke in the San  Diego union-tribune  the fact is that the case began when  Morgan Cooke published an article in the  UT I read that article I discussed it  with Emily Allen and then mark Conover I  went to the FBI and we said look at this  is there a case and after that we went  we consulted with people in DOJ who in  this administration made the decision  you know to indict representative hunk  hunter nothing  have been more apolitical than the  process that was involved here in fact  today in many ways is a triumph for the  press and shows the importance of having  a free press that not only can the  people rely on but that the Department  of Justice can turn to for guidance Cook  was one of the reporters outside the  courthouse and was stunned to hear what  the prosecutor had to say about her I  think that's what I heard but that  doesn't sound like something that I  would hear very much caught off-guard  because usually and when people call us  out it's not to tell us a great job we  did and how much we helped and how  important we are it Cook became an  overnight journalism sensation her  reporting cited by the networks and  national newspapers a major career break  I think it would take a lot for me to  leave San Diego I think I could still  learn a lot here I can still grow here I  can still do the work that I'm capable  of here and it's a really special  newsroom because everyone is on everyone  else's team and they helped carry me if  I could do it better with help they  contributed their skill and I've just  been really lucky to be in a newsroom  where I have colleagues who support me  and support this work and are willing to  give what they can to to that and that's  our program for tonight thanks for  joining us we'll see you back here next  week
 

